.TH SET_REALLOC 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
set_realloc \- Reallocate a set to make more space

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/set.h>

.IB int
.IB set_realloc(set_t* set);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBset_realloc\fR function reallocates a set to make more space. It takes one argument: the set to reallocate. The function returns 1 if the set is successfully reallocated, and 0 if the set is invalid.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB set
The set to reallocate.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns 1 if the set is successfully reallocated, and 0 if the set is invalid.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBset_realloc\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/set.h>

int main() {
    set_t set;
    set_init(&set);

    set_inserts(&set, "apple");
    set_inserts(&set, "banana");
    set_inserts(&set, "cherry");

    printf("Original set length: %u\n", set.len);

    if(set_realloc(&set)) {
        printf("Set reallocated successfully\n");
        printf("New set length: %u\n", set.len);
    } else {
        printf("Failed to reallocate set\n");
    }

    set_free(&set);
    return 0;
}
.nef